"d" <someone@microsoft.com> wrote:
>If you are looking to even the field so to speak, why not just make the
>desirable artifacts crappier?

The problem is not that the desirable artifacts are so much better
than the undesirable ones so much as that the undesirable ones are
not significantly more desirable than a good non-artifact weapon.
Nerfing Mjollnir, Excalibur, Stormbringer, Frost Brand, and Grayswandir
would not make the game significantly more enjoyable, but it would
make it harder.  Adding interesting powers to the currently-poor
artifacts would make the game more interesting.

(Although... I think there is an argument for nerfing Grayswandir;
it's already a silver saber that gives hallucination resistance,
so +1d8 would be a perfectly adequate damage bonus; there's no need
for it to have double-damage.)
